@startuml
title A — Main path: durable admission, push, application ACK
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 210
participant "Bank service\n+ source outbox" as Bank
participant "Notification API\n+ Outbox Relay" as API
database "PostgreSQL\nledger" as DB
queue "Kafka" as K
participant "Coordinator\n+ Scheduler" as C
participant "Push adapter" as W
participant "Push provider" as P
participant "Customer app" as App
participant "Receipt API" as R
Bank -> API: POST notification (business_key)
API -> DB: Commit notification + outbox\nunique business_key, sync replica ACK
DB --> API: notification_id
API --> Bank: 202 accepted (notification_id)
API -> K: Publish committed request
K -> C: critical.requested (may be repeated)
C -> DB: Inbox dedupe + route + durable next_action_at
C -> DB: Lock state; create push attempt + command outbox
API -> K: Relay push command (stable attempt_id)
K -> W: Send command (at-least-once)
W -> DB: Validate state/version; acquire send-permit
DB --> W: Permit + stable provider key
W -> P: Send push (notification_id; short TTL)
P --> W: Accepted + provider_message_id
W -> DB: Record accepted unless already delivered
note over W,DB: Provider acceptance is not delivery.
P -> App: Deliver notification to app
App -> R: Authenticated app ACK (notification_id)
R -> DB: Transaction: dedupe receipt; DELIVERED + evidence
DB --> R: Commit
R --> App: ACK persisted
C -> DB: Scheduler/reconciler sees terminal state
note over C,DB: No new send-permits after durable evidence.
@enduml
